ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57): a one-row code-block gets the second row the decoders write
Library: openjph 0.32.0
Fixes: CVE-2026-111151
Upstream: none yet: no fix on master as of 2026-10-21 (ours)
Remove when: a release fixes CVE-2026-111151 (OSV), or this patch no longer applies

The HT block decoders (generic, SSSE3, AVX2, VSX, WASM) write the cleanup pass two rows at a
time. A precinct one sample high (ycb_prime = 0) makes code-blocks one row high, whose buffer
held one row: the second row was written past it, into the next allocation (heap
out-of-bounds write from any .jph, .j2c or HTJ2K-compressed EXR). Code-block buffers now hold
an even number of rows; the decoders read back only cb_size.h of them.

diff --git a/src/core/codestream/ojph_codeblock.cpp b/src/core/codestream/ojph_codeblock.cpp
index a24be39..1cd5124 100644
--- a/src/core/codestream/ojph_codeblock.cpp
+++ b/src/core/codestream/ojph_codeblock.cpp
@@ -61,11 +61,14 @@ namespace ojph {
       assert(byte_alignment / sizeof(ui32) > 1);
       const ui32 f = byte_alignment / sizeof(ui32) - 1;
       ui32 stride = (nominal.w + f) & ~f; // a multiple of 8
+      // the block decoders write rows in pairs, so a one-row codeblock
+      // (a precinct one sample high) needs a second row
+      ui32 rows = (nominal.h + 1) & ~1u;
 
       if (precision <= 32)
-        allocator->pre_alloc_data<ui32>(nominal.h * (size_t)stride, 0);
+        allocator->pre_alloc_data<ui32>(rows * (size_t)stride, 0);
       else
-        allocator->pre_alloc_data<ui64>(nominal.h * (size_t)stride, 0);
+        allocator->pre_alloc_data<ui64>(rows * (size_t)stride, 0);
     }
 
     //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
@@ -80,7 +83,8 @@ namespace ojph {
 
       const ui32 f = byte_alignment / sizeof(ui32) - 1;
       this->stride = (nominal.w + f) & ~f; // a multiple of 8
-      this->buf_size = this->stride * nominal.h;
+      // an even number of rows, as in pre_alloc()
+      this->buf_size = this->stride * ((nominal.h + 1) & ~1u);
 
       if (precision <= 32) {
         this->precision = BUF32;
